<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A1316027002">
<title>
IAT Sensor-1
</title>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
The MAF sensor with IAT sensor-1 will be damaged if it is exposed to a temperature higher than 100 &#176;C (212 &#176;F).
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Do not heat the MAF sensor with IAT sensor-1 to a temperature higher than 100 &#176;C (212 &#176;F).
</ptxt>
</attention4>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove MAF sensor with IAT sensor-1. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1316026"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check sensor O-ring (1) for damage and deterioration. If faulty condition is found, replace MAF sensor with IAT sensor-1.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check that resistance between sensor terminals varies depending on temperature while blowing hot air to temperature sensing part (2) of MAF sensor with IAT sensor-1 (3) using hot air drier (4).
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If faulty condition is found, replace MAF sensor with IAT sensor-1.
</ptxt>
